The two cleanest modern ways to center a div are **Flexbox** and **CSS Grid**:

### Method 1: CSS Grid (Shortest & Cleanest)
```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  height: 100vh; /* or any height */
}
```

### Method 2: Flexbox
```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center; /* horizontal */
  align-items: center;     /* vertical */
  height: 100vh;
}
```
Both methods are Baseline widely available across all modern browsers.

Here is a sleek modern pricing card with glassmorphic styling and hover animations:

```html
<div class="pricing-card">
  <span class="badge">Most Popular</span>
  <h3 class="plan-title">Pro Plan</h3>
  <div class="price">$29<span>/month</span></div>
  <ul class="feature-list">
    <li>✓ Unlimited AI chat requests</li>
    <li>✓ Full HTML & code generation</li>
    <li>✓ Priority neural processing</li>
    <li>✓ 24/7 dedicated support</li>
  </ul>
  <button class="pricing-btn">Subscribe Now</button>
</div>

<style>
  .pricing-card {
    background: #222;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 32px 24px;
    max-width: 320px;
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.25s, box-shadow 0.25s;
  }
  .pricing-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(16, 163, 127, 0.2);
  }
  .badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: -12px;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    background: #10a37f;
    color: #fff;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .price {
    font-size: 40px;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }
  .price span {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #888;
  }
  .feature-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 20px 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .feature-list li {
    padding: 8px 0;
    color: #ccc;
  }
  .pricing-btn {
    width: 100%;
    background: #10a37f;
    color: #fff;
    border: none;
    padding: 12px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>
```

Here is a clean, modern, and responsive dark-mode navigation bar using semantic HTML5 and flexbox CSS:

```html
<nav class="navbar">
  <div class="nav-brand">El GPT 1.0</div>
  <ul class="nav-links">
    <li><a href="#home" class="active">Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="#features">Features</a></li>
    <li><a href="#pricing">Pricing</a></li>
    <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
  </ul>
  <button class="nav-cta">Get Started</button>
</nav>

<style>
  .navbar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 16px 32px;
    background-color: #1a1a1a;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
  }
  .nav-brand {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #10a37f;
  }
  .nav-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .nav-links a {
    color: #a0a0a0;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 15px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  .nav-links a:hover, .nav-links a.active {
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .nav-cta {
    background-color: #10a37f;
    color: #ffffff;
    border: none;
    padding: 8px 18px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }
  .nav-cta:hover {
    background-color: #0d8265;
  }
</style>
```

